__________________________________________
class ChatRequest(BaseModel):
    message: str

BaseModel kya hai?  BaseModel Pydantic ka base class hai.

Hum keh rahe hain: "Pydantic, mujhe ek data structure define karna hai jiska naam ChatRequest hai. Iske andar jo incoming data aayega usme message naam ka field hona chahiye aur uski type str honi chahiye."
class ChatResponse(BaseModel):
    response: str
    Ye incoming request nahi, balki hamare API ka output structure define karta hai.

Humne endpoint mein:
    @app.post("/chat", response_model=ChatResponse)  likha hai.
      Meaning:  /chat endpoint jo response return karega, uska expected structure ChatResponse hai.
      
Ye sirf data schema/model hai.Naam ChatRequest humne diya because this represents the data expected by our /chat API.

