"I separated the API layer from application services so that retrieval, LLM interaction, and 
memory management remain independently testable and maintainable."

__________________________________________ X __________________________________________
_load_vector_store()
The underscore is a convention meaning:
"This is an internal/helper method; users of this service normally shouldn't call it directly."

Literal["tutor", "quiz", "interview"]

Pydantic says:
Only these three values are allowed.

And:   = "tutor"  means Tutor is the default.
This is input validation at the API boundary.